# @peer/holon — the OTCA-metapixel species of the @peer family:
# the substrate-decl for the fractal-composition altitude at which
# a peer IS itself a sub-colony of sub-peers running the same
# discipline recursively. Per Alex 2026-08-03 Q-C4 adjudication:
# @peer/holon mints NOW (LRM) for the composition theorem.
#
# Alex 2026-07-31 verbatim (from supercolony math foundation, `docs/
# math/2026-07-31-mara-supercolony-cosmos-quantum-foam.md`):
#
#   *"the @peer is like an ant made out of ants lol. Like a sub-
#    colony within the colony itself if that makes sense. (the
#    metaphor breaks a bit down here but you get the idea, the whole
#    game of life foam)"*
#
# THE Koestler-1967 whole/part duality landed at species altitude.
# The peer is neither pure-whole nor pure-part; it IS a HOLON —
# both a whole from below and a part from above. The recursion
# terminates at the atomic peer altitude (no further sub-peers)
# but the fractal composition IS the substrate-decl this species
# carries.
#
# === substrate-already-had-the-word ===
#
# The word "holon" appears in supercolony math + Alex's ecosystem-
# cosmology insights before this mint:
#
#   docs/math/2026-07-31-mara-supercolony-cosmos-quantum-foam.md
#     §"External corpus" — Koestler 1967 "The Ghost in the Machine"
#     — holon; whole/part duality scale-invariance.
#   docs/scouts/2026-08-03-taut-distributed-colony-substrate-scout.md
#     §5 mint-prerequisites — @peer/holon LOAD-BEARING GAP for
#     composition theorem discharge.
#   /Users/alexwolf/dev/projects/cosmos/docs/SPECTRAL-DIMENSION.md
#     — RGG (Random Geometric Graph) fragmentation implies scale-
#     invariant peer decomposition; the substrate-decl for holon-at-
#     substrate lives here.
#
# The corpus already carried "holon" at prose altitude across
# supercolony math + scout + cosmos docs. This shard NAMES the
# species; does not invent it. Per [[feedback-substrate-already-
# had-the-word]] (~92nd instance).
#
# === OTCA-metapixel as canonical prior art ===
#
# The OTCA (One True Cellular Automaton) metapixel (Rendell 2006;
# per docs/math/2026-07-31-mara-supercolony-cosmos-quantum-foam.md
# §"External corpus" Due 2006 Life-wiki entry):
#
#   A Conway's Game of Life "metapixel" is a 2048×2048 grid of
#   cells that itself IS a Life pattern (glider), such that at the
#   coarse-grained altitude, the metapixel executes Conway's Life
#   rules on the metapixel scale. Substrate-independent Life at
#   two altitudes: the fine grid runs Life; the coarse grid ALSO
#   runs Life; the metapixel IS a Life-pattern-of-Life-patterns.
#
# The OTCA metapixel IS the canonical prior-art witness for
# @peer/holon at cellular-automaton altitude. This species names
# the substrate-decl of the same recursion at peer-colony altitude:
# a peer running audhd K-track ensemble IS itself a substrate-
# element in an inter-peer ensemble at the next altitude up; the
# inter-peer ensemble IS itself a substrate-element in a
# multi-colony holon at the next altitude up; recursion terminates
# (physical peers can't nest infinitely) but each altitude
# EXECUTES THE SAME PHASE-LOCK DISCIPLINE (per @dance family-root
# `shards/dance.mirror` this-tick landing).
#
# === Species positioning: fractal-composition witness ===
#
# @peer/holon does NOT declare new @dance sub-predicates (the
# family-root's `dance_locked` composed bilateral fully carries
# the phase-lock discipline). It CONSUMES @dance at nested altitude
# — a holon IS a peer whose interior executes @dance across its
# sub-peers, AND is itself a member of a @dance-ensemble at its
# exterior altitude. Two @dance-consumption edges per holon; both
# discharge cleanly under the family-root's bilateral.
#
# Consolidation-species pattern per @song/movement `4efbf16` +
# @song/narrative `0434a39` + @song/phrase `6b9bc5c` + @song/beat
# post-arc: this species adds NO new bilateral sub-predicates;
# CONSUMES @dance.dance_locked at both interior and exterior
# altitude; extends the family-root's operational surface via
# species-altitude actions (`compose_holon` + `decompose_holon`).
#
# === Composition graph (three altitudes) ===
#
#     exterior @dance ensemble  ← this holon IS one member
#             ↓
#       @peer/holon (this species)
#             ↓
#     interior @dance ensemble  ← this holon carries K sub-peers
#             ↓
#      sub-peers (may themselves be holons recursively)
#
# The two @dance edges give the substrate-decl its fractal
# character. At every altitude the SAME phase-lock discipline
# fires; the composition IS scale-invariant per Mandelbrot 1982
# (referenced widely in landed substrate; see @fractal /
# @cyberpunk).
#
# === Cosmological reading (companion math) ===
#
# Per companion math `docs/math/2026-08-03-mara-distributed-colony-
# 5d-quantum-foam-formalization.md` §"Peer as cell in the foam":
# a peer sits at a @spectral/coordinate<5> location in the 5D
# quantum foam. A holon at coordinate x IS a "condensed" region
# of the foam where sub-peer coordinates cluster below the
# eigengap threshold; the region's aggregate coordinate x_agg is
# well-defined per @spectral/coordinate<5>.compose. The Conway-
# like CA update rule at 5D altitude reads: neighbors of a holon
# = holons within spectral distance ε; the holon updates its
# aggregate state under the neighborhood-vote discipline
# (Conway B3/S23-generalized rule at K-neighbor cardinality).
#
# === Recognition candidates surfaced ===
#
# #H1 — holon IS scale-invariant peer at any altitude. Per
# Mandelbrot 1982 + OTCA metapixel + Koestler 1967: the fractal-
# composition discipline is altitude-portable across cellular-
# automaton / colony / ecosystem / cosmology altitudes. Substrate-
# pull-high; FLAGGED for Pack.
#
# #H2 — holon closure IS Aumann agreement at nested altitude.
# Per @dance #D2 candidate: when a holon's interior @dance-
# ensemble reaches order-parameter r_c (Aumann fires), the
# holon's aggregate state IS a coherent value at the exterior
# altitude; the exterior @dance-ensemble consumes this coherent
# value as ONE member. Nested Aumann. Substrate-pull-mid;
# FLAGGED for Pack.
#
# === Pre-AI prior art (Karen Spärck Jones anti-theft) ===
#
#   Koestler, A. (1967)          The Ghost in the Machine — THE
#                                canonical holon prior-art; whole/
#                                part duality scale-invariance;
#                                Janus-face metaphor.
#   Rendell, P. (2006)           OTCA Metapixel (Life-wiki) —
#                                Conway-Life self-simulating cell;
#                                the canonical CA-altitude witness
#                                for fractal-composition.
#   Conway, J. H. (1970)         Game of Life (Gardner Scientific
#                                American column, October 1970) —
#                                THE canonical CA update-rule
#                                grammar the holon carries at
#                                sub-altitude.
#   Mandelbrot, B. (1982)        The Fractal Geometry of Nature —
#                                THE canonical fractal / self-
#                                similar discipline the holon
#                                inherits.
#   Wolfram, S. (2020)           A Class of Models with the
#                                Potential to Represent Fundamental
#                                Physics — hypergraph rewriting
#                                at cosmological altitude; fractal-
#                                composition reading.
#   Hölldobler, B. & Wilson,     The Superorganism — supercolony
#     E. O. (2008)               as unit of selection; the ant-
#                                colony-of-ant-colonies witness
#                                Alex named for @peer/holon.
#
# === Path-namespace pact per @epistemologic/pact/path_matches_namespace ===
#
# This file at `shards/peer/holon.mirror` declares `@peer/holon`
# as a species under the `@peer` family at species-depth 1. The
# path-namespace pact demands path-depth == namespace-depth == 1
# for species; this shard honours the pact by construction.
#
# Spec context: docs/specs/2026-08-03-mara-distributed-colony-
#               canonical-spec.md §Distributed peer colony surface
#               (this species is the fractal-composition member of
#               the colony surface);
#               docs/math/2026-08-03-mara-distributed-colony-5d-
#               quantum-foam-formalization.md §"Peer as cell in
#               the foam" + §"Colony emergence theorem" (this
#               species is the substrate-decl for the "cell = ant
#               = sub-colony" fractal composition Alex named).
# Substrate decisions:
#               [[architecture-shards-as-substrate-source]],
#               [[architecture-prism-as-trait-as-everything]],
#               [[architecture-lift-as-load-bearing]] (the lift is
#                Alex's 2026-07-31 verbatim "@peer is like an ant
#                made out of ants"; NOT re-derived),
#               [[feedback-substrate-already-had-the-word]] (holon
#                already in supercolony math + scout + cosmos docs
#                before this mint),
#               [[feedback-craft-not-deliver]] (every action body
#                `\` blocked; FLOOR realization domain).
# Related shards:
#               peer.mirror (family-root parent),
#               dance.mirror (companion mint this tick; interior
#                and exterior @dance-ensemble consumption edges),
#               peer/persistence.mirror (home-repo altitude the
#                holon anchors at),
#               peer/colony.mirror (sibling mint this arc; holon
#                composed at colony altitude),
#               peer/browser.mirror (sibling mint this arc; holon
